~ approach_fire
Narrator: As you approach voices drift over you. 
Old Man 1: Oh ho ho ho, so you dont know do ya. 
Old Man 2: Well I've got some words for you. 
Old Man 3: Blimy, boys, the beans are [wave]burnin[/wave].  
Narrator:  You quietly make your way through the stiff bluestem grass. Finally reaching the clearing, you peak your head around a corner. Three grizzled grizzled panhandlers are sitting around a cast-iron pot thats bubbling away. They are arguing about who should have been watching the beans.
Old Man 1: I told yous was tending to my bunion. 
Old Man 2: [shake]DAMN[/shake] your bunion Joe. 
Old Man 3: Blimy boys, don't bicker. The beans are still burning.   
Narrator: The beans, in fact, were still burning. 
Narrator: They finally quieted down, found an stick, and began stirring the poor beans. 
Narrator: One of them pulled out some old metal mugs and the feasting began. 
Narrator: You are famished. [wait=0.2] Are you afraid of them? 
- Yes. 
	Narrator: Poor thing. Perhaps fear will fill your tummy. 
- No. 
	Narrator: Atta' boy.  
Narrator: What will you do?
~ get_beans
- Make a move for the pot.
	Narrator: You step quietly over to the pot, where it is sitting behind their backs. You gingerly reach your hands towards it. 
	You: [pulse]OW[/pulse]
	Narrator: [shake][color=red]It's burning remember? [/shake]
	Old Man 1: Looks like we got a little thief!
	Old Man 3: Blimy boys, the night just gets better and better. 
	Old Man 2: [shake]Grab him.[/shake]
	Old Man 2: Looks like we found the weany for our beans. Cut him up. 
	=> death
	
- Ask politely. 
	You: Excuse me. 
	Old Man 1: [shake]**Burb**[/shake] these are some [b]good[/b] beans boys.
	Old Man 2: Mghh, they need some weanies. Can't have beanies without weanies. 
	Old Man 3: Shut your trap. All you do is complain. 
	Narrator: **they didn't hear you**
